  "title": "Col. Baeterrae",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 15 A3 Col. Baeterrae",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: settlement and bridge at B\u00e9ziers. Prior to the Roman conquest, the local toponym seems to have been\u00a0Besara and the site was located in the territory of the Volcae Tectosages. The Romans annexed the site along with the rest of Transalpine Gaul. A colony for veterans of Levio VII was established in A.D. 36.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Colonia Julia Baeterrae Septimanorum is located where the Via Herculia crosses the Orb river. It is now modern B\u00e9ziers, France. The site has been inhabited at least since 750-650 B.C.",
